## editor[¶](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/working-with/plugins/reference-for-showing-kanzi-engine-plugin-custom-types.html#editor "Link to this heading")
Sets the editor type Kanzi Studio users use to set the value for the property. If you do not set an editor, Kanzi assigns a default editor.
If you set the [valueProvider](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/working-with/plugins/reference-for-showing-kanzi-engine-plugin-custom-types.html#valueprovider) attribute to `PropertyType` or `StringList`, do not set the editor type. Kanzi Studio assigns the correct editor automatically.
For a list of Kanzi Studio property editors, see [Kanzi Studio property editors for property types declared in Kanzi Engine plugins](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/working-with/plugins/studio-editors.html).  
| **Syntax**  | `metadata.editor = "editor";`  |  
| --- | --- |  
| **Values**  |   
 | `editor`  | Kanzi Studio property editor name. See [Kanzi Studio property editors for property types declared in Kanzi Engine plugins](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/working-with/plugins/studio-editors.html).  |  
| --- | --- |  
 |  
| **Examples**  |  C++ 
