## defaultValue[¶](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/working-with/plugins/reference-for-showing-kanzi-engine-plugin-custom-types.html#defaultvalue "Link to this heading")
Sets the value to which Kanzi Studio sets the property when the property is added to a node or resource. Use this attribute to define the value to which the Kanzi Studio user most likely wants to set the property.
For example, for a boolean property type whose default value is `true`, set `metadata.defaultValue = "False";`. When the Kanzi Studio user adds that property type to a node, Kanzi Studio sets the property as disabled. This way, the user does not have to perform two actions.  
| **Syntax**  | `metadata.defaultValue = "value";`  |  
| --- | --- |  
| **Values**  |   
 | `value`  | The default value of the property or message in Kanzi Studio  |  
| --- | --- |  
 |  
| **Examples**  |  C++ 
```
// Set the default value of a string property in Kanzi Studio to video.mp4.
metadata.defaultValue = "video.mp4";

