## Creating a debug visualization for your 3D node type[¶](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/working-with/plugins/configuring-custom-components-for-kanzi-studio.html#creating-a-debug-visualization-for-your-3d-node-type "Link to this heading")
For your 3D node type, you can create a debug visualization that is visible in Kanzi Studio when the Preview is in the Analyze mode. Use debug visualizations to render information that is helpful while you develop your plugin.
To create a debug visualization for your 3D node type:
  1. Implement the function that draws the debug visualization that you want to render in the Preview.
  2. Use the `Module::registerDebugRenderingFunctions[](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/reference/kanzi-runtime-api/a15126.html#a72845cd876d34aff4d4b7740cb63bab0)` function to register the function that you use to draw debug visualizations in the plugin module. In this function, use the `DebugRenderRegistry::addMapping[](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/reference/kanzi-runtime-api/a13690.html#a4f57d9ea1f690914d81bc027e41edb5f)` function to map your 3D node type to the function that draws the debug visualization.
  3. To see the debug visualization in Kanzi Studio, in the Preview click ![analyze-off](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/_images/analyze-off.png) to enter the Analyze mode, right-click ![analyze-on](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/_images/analyze-on.png), and select Debug objects.


For an example of a debug visualization, see the [Node3D plugin example](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/examples/node3d-plugin/node3d-plugin.html).
