When you run the plugin, it creates in the Screen > RootNode node an Empty Node 2D node which is 300 pixels high and 400 pixels wide. The plugin names the Empty Node 2D node Empty Node 2D. You can extend this example by creating a Color Brush and use it to set the background color of the Empty Node 2D node by setting its Background Brush property to that Color Brush. See [Creating resources](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/working-with/plugins/reference-kanzi-studio-plugin-interface.html#creating-resources).
