### Observing application state[¶](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/working-with/application-configurations/application-configuration.html#observing-application-state "Link to this heading")
You can observe the application state to find out whether an application is running, minimized, or suspended.
A Kanzi application is always in one of these states:
  * `MainLoopState::Running[](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/reference/kanzi-runtime-api/a11119.html#ae35554056f5fa4e74b1d5d5921bf8ea4a5bda814c4aedb126839228f1a3d92f09)` state. This is the normal mode of operation of a Kanzi application. This is the initial state of an application.
  * `MainLoopState::Paused[](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/reference/kanzi-runtime-api/a11119.html#ae35554056f5fa4e74b1d5d5921bf8ea4ae99180abf47a8b3a856e0bcb2656990a)` state. The platform can impose rules on application behavior when it is out of focus or minimized. To mark such state, a platform backend can set the application to the `MainLoopState::Paused[](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/reference/kanzi-runtime-api/a11119.html#ae35554056f5fa4e74b1d5d5921bf8ea4ae99180abf47a8b3a856e0bcb2656990a)` state.
In this state, Kanzi stops normal input handling and rendering, and waits to be put back to the `MainLoopState::Running[](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/reference/kanzi-runtime-api/a11119.html#ae35554056f5fa4e74b1d5d5921bf8ea4a5bda814c4aedb126839228f1a3d92f09)` state. Additionally, it is typical for applications to halt heavy work when in this state.
  * `MainLoopState::Quitting[](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/reference/kanzi-runtime-api/a11119.html#ae35554056f5fa4e74b1d5d5921bf8ea4a9ccfee4c47009600237ea2b0145db1ec)` state. This state indicates that either application or the platform requested the application to quit by calling `MainLoopScheduler::quit[](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/reference/kanzi-runtime-api/a13618.html#a5721644f5c883f00374ba00d56c9dcd4)`. In this state, applications must avoid starting work, unless that work is related to uninitialization.


This diagram shows the states of a Kanzi application.
[![../../_images/states.svg](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/_images/states.svg)](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/_images/states.svg)
To find out the application state, call `MainLoopScheduler::getState[](https://docs.kanzi.com/4.1.0/en/reference/kanzi-runtime-api/a13618.html#ac883023118adc366a1f41d9f1e248125)`.
For example, to prevent adding a task when an application is quitting:

```
void doSomethingRepeatedly()
{
    doSomething();

    // If a condition is met...
    if (someCondition() &&
        // ...and the application is not quitting...
        getState() != MainLoopState::Quitting)
    {
        // ...add another task to the task dispatcher.
        getDomain()->getTaskDispatcher()->submit([this]()
                                                 {
                                                     this->doSomethingRepeatedly();
                                                 });
    }
}

```
